<title>FRANCE: France Telecom confirms 30 mln Ffr fine.</title>
<headline>France Telecom confirms 30 mln Ffr fine.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>France Telecom on Monday confirmed it had been fined a total of 30 million francs by the competition court for having made improper use of its monopoly position during a 1995 tender for a contract at insurer AXA.</p>
<p>British Telecom France had complained at the court, the highest body in France to rule on competition issues, that France Telecom unit Transpac had used below-cost prices for keeping the AXA contract, offering a 8.6 million franc discount.</p>
<p>&quot;We confirm that we have been fined,&quot; said a France Telecom spokesman. &quot;It is an old affair, from a time when we were still getting used to competition. We would do it differently nowadays,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
